# UI

Dark, dense draft HUD. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (`@theme inline`): `background`, `foreground`, `panel`, `panel-border`, `muted`, `accent`, `accent-dim`. Tailwind CSS v4 — no `tailwind.config.js`. Prefer those tokens over ad-hoc hex.

## Structure

- Pages in `src/app/` stay server components when they only read `params` / `searchParams`.
- Interactive surfaces are client components: `src/components/live-room.tsx`, `home-search.tsx`, `mock-drafts.tsx`, `coach-panel.tsx`.
- Live room polls `GET /api/drafts/:id/live?username=` about every 2s (`POLL_MS`). Keep the payload a snapshot; do not add client-side scoring.
- Named exports for components. Colocate a `*.test.tsx` when behavior matters (filters, clock copy, empty username, compare mode).

## Copy and product constraints

- The app does not make picks. Do not add a “draft this player” action that hits Sleeper.
- Username is required to open `/draft/[draftId]`. Mock tab still asks for a username so the seat can be resolved.
- Show ADP, ADP gap vs current pick, bye, injury, and last-year line when the snapshot has them.
- Position chips use `src/components/position-badge.tsx`.

## After live-room visual changes

Replace `docs/live-room.webp` (README autoplay) and update `docs/live-room.mp4` if you still have the source clip.
